  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "West keeps compounding at roughly its 10-year pace (~8% revenue CAGR FY2015-25). FY2026 lands at the raised guidance midpoint ($3.36B, 9.4% reported, 10-11% organic). From FY2027 growth stays high-single-digit on HVP components for biologics and injectable GLP-1s, and on the EU Annex 1 sterility upgrade cycle. That is partly offset in FY2027 by the remaining half-year of SmartDose 3.5mL roll-off and a lower-growth West Vantage contract-manufacturing segment. Mix shift toward HVP rebuilds pre-SBC EBITDA margin from 27.6% (GAAP basis, still carrying FY2026 SmartDose-exit restructuring) to 30.5%, which roughly matches Q2 2026 on an adjusted basis and stays short of the FY2021 COVID-vaccine peak of 32.2%. Capex falls from the guided 7.8% of sales to a 6% maintenance-plus-growth level as the GLP-1 capacity build completes.",
    "bull": "The bull axes are GLP-1 and Annex 1. Injectable GLP-1 adoption is still early-stage, as management says, and HVP GLP-1 components keep growing in the high teens. Biologics organic growth (29% in Q2 2026) holds above 15%. The ~6 billion-component Annex 1 opportunity converts Standard Products to higher-spec HVP at higher price points. Revenue grows 10%+ through FY2029, and margin reaches 33% as HVP rises from ~64% of sales toward 75%, above the FY2021 peak. Regulatory switching costs protect each design win for the life of the drug.",
    "bear": "The bear axes are concentration and the delivery format. A small set of GLP-1 makers are a large share of incremental demand. Oral semaglutide/orforglipron formulations and GLP-1 price cuts slow injectable volume growth, while pharma customers destock as they did in FY2023-24, when revenue fell 2% and EBITDA margin compressed ~5pp. Growth drops to 4-5% after FY2026, the capacity built for GLP-1 runs under-utilized, and margin stalls at 27.5%. The market's ~40x forward multiple de-rates; the terminal is capped at 16x."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "West is a high-quality, regulatory-moated compounder: its components are written into drug filings, so customers rarely switch. At a price near the 52-week high the market is paying for sustained high-single to low-double-digit growth plus margin recovery. The DCF charges SBC and withholding taxes as cash, holds the share count flat (buybacks fund it), and treats working capital as a use of cash for a manufacturer. It caps the terminal at 20x owner FCF for the base and bull cases.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "GLP-1 concentration: a few drug makers drive much of the HVP growth, and oral formulations could cut injectable volumes.",
      "Customer destocking cycles like FY2023-24 swing revenue and margin hard, since the business has high operating leverage.",
      "Terminal value is most of the value, so the result is sensitive to WACC: each 1pp on the discount rate moves base value by roughly 15-20%.",
      "Capex intensity: if the GLP-1/biologics capacity build keeps capex near the FY2023-24 12-13% instead of normalizing to ~6-7%, owner FCF falls well short of this path.",
      "SmartDose divestiture after-tax proceeds are estimated; the gain and its tax were not disclosed in the data at hand."
    ]
  },
